 ### [Training Objective and Densification](7448-training-objective-and-densification.md)
-This method defines the loss functions and densification protocols for **MeshGS**, a variant of 3D Gaussian Splatting that aligns primitives with an explicit mesh surface. It solves the problem of Gaussian splats drifting away from geometry or expanding uncontrollably by introducing surface-aware regularization and projection losses. It differs from standard 3DGS [22] by splitting the primitive population into **tightly-bound** ($G^t$) and **loosely-bound** ($G^l$) sets, applying distinct densification rules and loss terms to each, and enforcing proximity to the mesh surface.
