 ### Interleaved Densification
-- [S2] Alternates between spatial and temporal densification every 2 epochs to avoid Gaussians failing to reconstruct either motion or appearance detail. This is particularly relevant for dynamic scenes where spatio-temporal optimization is required.
+- **Step:** Alternates between spatial and temporal densification every 2 epochs to avoid Gaussians failing to reconstruct either motion or appearance detail [S2]. This is necessary because deciding whether a Gaussian needs spatial or temporal densification at every iteration can lead to failure in reconstructing either aspect [S2].
 
 ### Two-Stage Training Scheme for FWD-U
-- [S3] A training strategy that decouples depth network initialization from full model training to improve stability and performance.
-- **Step:** Stage 1: Construct RGB point clouds for each input view. Project the constructed point clouds to the target view using the differentiable point cloud renderer. Aggregate all point clouds from the various input views to render RGB images at the target view. Optimize the depth network using a photometric loss between the rendered target views and the ground truth target images. Stage 2: Freeze or continue training the initialized depth network and jointly train the entire model (spatial feature network, MLP, renderer, transformer, refinement module).
-- **Parameter:** Performance improvement: approximately 0.4 dB PSNR gain.
-- **Pitfall:** Jointly training the depth network and other components from scratch causes instability.
+- **Definition:** A training strategy that decouples depth network initialization from full model training to improve stability and performance [S3]. The intuition is that jointly training the depth network and other components from scratch is unstable [S3].
